Third-party notice: VST 3 headers

This repository redistributes the VST 3 C API headers, under GPLv3. They are
the contents of include/vst3, taken verbatim from
https://github.com/steinbergmedia/vst3_c_api at commit 453015e (tagged
v3.7.13_build_42 and v3.7.14_build_55), and they remain under Steinberg Media
Technologies GmbH's dual license: the proprietary VST 3 License Agreement, or
the GNU General Public License v3. include/vst3/LICENSE.txt is that license,
carried with them.

Of the two, only the GPLv3 permits this. The proprietary license forbids
distributing the SDK "in parts or its entirety" without a signed agreement, so
this redistribution is made under the GPLv3 alternative, and the copy of the
headers you receive from this repository comes to you under the GPLv3.

The MIT license above covers this project's own source only. MIT is
GPL-compatible, so a combined work remains distributable, but a compiled VST 3
plug-in is such a combined work, and the terms under which you may distribute a
binary are determined by whichever Steinberg license you have accepted. Without
a signed VST 3 License Agreement, that is the GPLv3, and your distributed
plug-in must comply with it. That was already true before the headers were
vendored -- a plug-in built against them was always a combined work. What
changed is that this repository now hands you the headers rather than pointing
a submodule at them. "VST" is a trademark of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH.
